# Ferry Albatros, captain's cabin (C3, contract 34), 9 x 7, interior. column = i, row = j. The CAPTAIN (`capitan`) is seasick: he stands by his bunk, green and swaying.
# Talk to him: he asks for a hand (rub his back: YES / NO); after YES he feels better and gives the CORTADOR (bracelet module, flag 88, `setf mod_cortador`); flag 52 = the gift was given.
# Afterwards the ferry is ready to sail: leaving the ship (the deck mats) sets flag 53 and the ferry departs.
@map ferry_capitan
@size 9 7
@interior yes
@bg 3
@nofollow yes                   # contract 69: the follower stays out of the ferry and the sea
@fill carpet
@spawn door 4 5 N
@flag captain_done 52
@legend
  .  tile=carpet
  W  tile=carpet object=pwall
  I  tile=carpet object=pwall
  b  tile=carpet object=bunk
  T  tile=carpet object=table
  l  tile=carpet object=lamp
  N  tile=carpet object=barrel
  C  tile=carpet npc=capitan id=captain face=S script=captain
  m  tile=mat
@grid
  WWWWWWWWW
  I.lT..b..
  I.....b..
  I...C....
  I.N......
  I........
  I...mm...
@warp m -> ferry_camarotes spawn=captain
@script captain npc
    npc_face_hero captain
    jf captain_done after
    say ferry.captain.sick
    ask ferry.captain.ask
    jv 0 1 rub
    say ferry.captain.no
    end
  rub:
    sfx confirm
    wait 400
    sfx confirm
    wait 400
    say ferry.captain.better
    setf mod_cortador
    sfx item
    say ferry.captain.got
    say ferry.captain.about
    setf captain_done
    end
  after:
    say ferry.captain.after
@end
